BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ardc-grants-january-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270116
SUMMARY:Deadline: ARDC: Amateur Radio and Digital Communications Grants (Ja
 nuary 2027 round)
DESCRIPTION:ARDC funds amateur radio\, wireless technology education\, and 
 communications research and development\, including software-defined radio
 \, mesh and packet networking\, and open RF tooling\, which puts it square
 ly at the transmission-art and community-network end of creative tech.\n\n
 Organisation: Amateur Radio Digital Communications (ARDC)\nLocation: USA-b
 ased funder\, worldwide reach. US 501(c)(3) nonprofits\, government agenci
 es\, schools and universities\, and international nonprofits and schools\;
  individuals\, collectives and radio clubs apply through a nonprofit fisca
 l sponsor.\nAward: No fixed range is stated on the apply page\, but ARDC's
  published 2026 grant portfolio shows awards from USD 1\,285 up to USD 258
 \,000 (for example GNU Radio 4 at USD 258\,000). No application fee.\nDura
 tion: Quarterly grant cycles (deadlines 15 January\, 1 April\, 1 July\, 1 
 September)\; evaluation takes 60 to 120 days.\n\nMore: https://www.ardc.ne
 t/apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.ardc.net/apply/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
LOCATION:USA-based funder\, worldwide reach. US 501(c)(3) nonprofits\, gove
 rnment agencies\, schools and universities\, and international nonprofits 
 and schools\; individuals\, collectives and radio clubs apply through a no
 nprofit fiscal sponsor.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mit-solve-global-challenges-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261103
SUMMARY:Deadline: MIT Solve: 2027 Global Challenges
DESCRIPTION:MIT Solve's annual open innovation call selects tech-based solu
 tions to global challenges and backs them with funding and a nine-month su
 pport program. The 2027 cycle runs five parallel challenges on a shared ap
 plication deadline: the Global Climate Challenge\, Global Health Challenge
 \, Global Learning Challenge\, Global Economic Prosperity Challenge\, and 
 the Indigenous Communities Fellowship.\n\nOrganisation: MIT Solve (Massach
 usetts Institute of Technology)\nLocation: Remote\, worldwide. Nine-month 
 virtual support program with event attendance and media exposure opportuni
 ties.\nAward: Every selected Solver team receives a USD 10\,000 grant fund
 ed by Solve\, plus access to a pool of over USD 1 million in prize funding
  at selection and additional funding opportunities throughout the program.
  Sponsor prizes range from USD 100\,000 to 200\,000\, including the AI for
  Humanity Prize (up to USD 150\,000\, Patrick J. McGovern Foundation)\, th
 e Collegium Prize for Innovation (USD 100\,000)\, the Citizens Workforce I
 nnovation Prize (USD 100\,000)\, the Crescent Enterprises AI for Social In
 novation Prize (USD 100\,000) and the Seeding the Future Prize (USD 150\,0
 00). No application fee.\nDuration: Nine-month support program\, plus perm
 anent Solver status with ongoing access to future opportunities.\n\nMore: 
 https://solve.mit.edu/challenges?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://solve.mit.edu/challenges?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, worldwide. Nine-month virtual support program with event 
 attendance and media exposure opportunities.
END:VEVENT
