DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: NLnet Foundation: Open Call November 2026 (Restack\, Code
 Supply and general fund)
DESCRIPTION:NLnet's current open call funds open-source technical developme
 nt: software and hardware released under free licenses. ROUTES: the Restac
 k fund (open internet stack)\, the CodeSupply fund\, and the general open 
 call for everything else\; accessibility and assistive-tech FOSS (screen r
 eaders\, a11y tooling\, accessible interfaces) was repeatedly funded under
  the predecessor NGI Zero programme and fits...\n\nOrganisation: Stichting
  NLnet (with European Commission backing\; successor to the NGI Zero progr
 amme)\nLocation: Remote / worldwide. Individuals\, informal collectives\, 
 nonprofits\, SMEs and universities from any country\; EU-backed funds want
  a European dimension\, and applicants outside Horizon Europe countries mu
 st explain the fit.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 to 50\,000 for a first grant\, scal
 able in follow-ups\; the Restack fund alone will award EUR 7 million throu
 gh 2030. No application fee.\nDuration: Project-based\, typically up to ab
 out 12 months per plan\; calls recur roughly every two months.\n\nMore: ht
 tps://nlnet.nl/propose/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://nlnet.nl/propose/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Remote / worldwide. Individuals\, informal collectives\, nonprofit
 s\, SMEs and universities from any country\; EU-backed funds want a Europe
 an dimension\, and applicants outside Horizon Europe countries must explai
 n the fit.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mensch-maschine-visit-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART:20261201T222900Z
DTEND:20261201T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Fellowship 2027
 : Energy Ghosts (E-WERK Luckenwalde / Akademie der Künste)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nThe Mensch Maschine VISIT R
 esidency Program is an annual fellowship offering four fully funded fellow
 ships to artists from around the world\, run by the JUNGE AKADEMIE of the 
 Akademie der Künste (Berlin) with VISIT\, the artist-in-residence program
 me of the E.ON Foundation\, E-WERK Luckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centr
 e for Contemporary Art (Warsaw).\n\nOrganisation: JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Ak
 ademie der Künste\, VISIT (E.ON Foundation)\, E-WERK Luckenwalde and Ujaz
 dowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art\nLocation: E-WERK Luckenwalde\, 
 Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademie der Künste\, Berlin (1 fel
 low)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CCA in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to
  artists worldwide.\nAward: Four fully funded fellowships of EUR 20\,000 e
 ach\, intended for artist fees and production costs of a new project (rese
 arch and development\, travel\, materials and presentation costs)\, plus s
 tudio space and accommodation for the three-month residency.\nDuration: Th
 ree months\, roughly September to November 2027 (the AdK notice gives mid-
 August to mid-November)\; fellows must live and work on site at least 75% 
 of the time.\n\nMore: https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-maschin
 e-stipendium?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademi
 e der Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CC
 A in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:zoud-gamelab-finlit-game-jam-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Zoud GameLab 2026: Global Game Jam financial-literacy jam
  (prize and funding pool up to USD 140\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Zoud GameLab is a month-long virtual game jam run by Global Gam
 e Jam and Zoud\, the UAE's national financial wellbeing initiative\, under
  the theme Make FinLit Fun. Participants build a game that integrates fina
 ncial literacy in a meaningful way\; this is part of the judging criteria\
 , and a scoring rubric is published on the jam page.\n\nOrganisation: Zoud
  (UAE National Financial Wellbeing and Sustainability Initiative) with Glo
 bal Game Jam\nLocation: Online\, worldwide. Open to participants aged 18 a
 nd over in any country\; solo developers\, teams of any size and studios.\
 nAward: Shared prize and development-support funding pool of up to USD 140
 \,000 across best overall game\, runner-up\, third place\, financial-liter
 acy impact\, regional perspective\, compelling gameplay and a Best Game fr
 om the UAE award\; individual prize amounts are not published. No entry fe
 e.\nDuration: Month-long online jam\, 15 October to 15 November 2026\; win
 ners announced December 2026.\n\nMore: https://itch.io/jam/zoud-gamelab?ut
 m_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://itch.io/jam/zoud-gamelab?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online\, worldwide. Open to participants aged 18 and over in any c
 ountry\; solo developers\, teams of any size and studios.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rhizome-microgrants-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261120
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261121
SUMMARY:Deadline: Rhizome Microgrants 2026 (USD 500-1\,500 for digital art 
 and networked culture projects)
DESCRIPTION:Rhizome's annual microgrants\, running since 2014\, fund new cr
 eative projects related to digital art and networked culture\, especially 
 web-based works. Past awardees include a multilingual archive of printed "
 Internet directory" books\, a browser-based adventure game about caring fo
 r "small but alive" creatures\, and a free pop-up school in Portland.\n\nO
 rganisation: Rhizome\nLocation: Online. Open call for web-based and networ
 ked projects\; no location requirement is stated in the announcement.\nAwa
 rd: USD 500 to 1\,500 per project. Additional annual grants through the Te
 rrell Davis fund (with Joygill Moriah and LVLZ Healing Hub) for work speak
 ing to Black and Afrodiasporic experiences\; projects in any category can 
 opt in.\nDuration: Per project.\n\nMore: https://microgrants.rhizome.org/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://microgrants.rhizome.org/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online. Open call for web-based and networked projects\; no locati
 on requirement is stated in the announcement.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ssn-small-research-grants-2026-27@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: Surveillance Studies Network: Small Research Grants 2026-
 27 (up to GBP 1\,500)
DESCRIPTION:The Surveillance Studies Network\, the scholarly charity behind
  the journal Surveillance & Society\, funds small research activities in s
 urveillance studies\, including work on surveillance technologies\, data\,
  biometrics and AI-driven monitoring. Grants can cover costs such as trans
 cription\, participant payments\, travel\, equipment or conference fees.\n
 \nOrganisation: Surveillance Studies Network (SSN)\nLocation: Worldwide\, 
 with preference for researchers based in economically under-resourced regi
 ons (priority to UN-ranked Least Developed Countries). Applied by email\; 
 no travel required to apply.\nAward: Up to GBP 1\,500 per project\, plus a
  two-year SSN membership. The 2025-26 round made two awards. No applicatio
 n fee.\nDuration: Funds to be spent during the 2026-27 academic year\, by 
 5 January 2028.\n\nMore: https://surveillance-studies.net/honours/ssn-smal
 l-research-grants/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://surveillance-studies.net/honours/ssn-small-research-grants/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide\, with preference for researchers based in economically 
 under-resourced regions (priority to UN-ranked Least Developed Countries).
  Applied by email\; no travel required to apply.
END:VEVENT
